 SC LAB M2-L2: SECURE THE DMZ
 Pod: {{ pod_name }} ({{ prefix }})
 Gateway: http://{{ gw_ip }}
============================================================

SCENARIO:
ACS Consulting has a public web server that was accidentally
placed on the INTERNAL LAN at {{ gw_ip | replace('.1', '.50') }}.
External visitors can reach it, but this means the web server
has full access to internal resources like DC01 and file shares.

YOUR TASKS:
1. Log into pfSense at http://{{ gw_ip }}

2. CREATE a DMZ zone:
   a. Navigate to Interfaces > Assignments
   b. Add a new interface (OPT1) and rename it "DMZ"
   c. Assign a DMZ subnet (e.g., {{ gw_ip | replace('.1', '.0') | replace('.0', '') }}.200.0/24)

3. UPDATE firewall rules:
   a. WAN > Allow HTTP/HTTPS to DMZ web server only
   b. DMZ > Allow web server to respond to requests
   c. DMZ > BLOCK all traffic from DMZ to LAN
   d. LAN > Allow management access to DMZ

4. UPDATE NAT rules:
   a. Change the port forward from LAN IP to DMZ IP
   b. Web server should now be at the DMZ address

5. VERIFY:
   [ ] Web server is accessible from WAN
   [ ] DMZ cannot reach internal LAN
   [ ] LAN can still manage DMZ
   [ ] DC01 and file shares are NOT accessible from DMZ

